C# Windows Forms Booking & Registration Management Systems

A collection of interactive C# Windows Forms Desktop Applications designed to handle complex business logic, input validations, conditional eligibility, and automated fee/cost calculations for hospitality, travel, vehicle rental, and academic registration domain models.

🌟 Key Features & Included Modules

This suite contains four core management applications built using C# and .NET Windows Forms:

1. 🏨 Hotel Room Booking System

Input Validation: Enforces strict constraints on guest age (18–90), stay duration (1–30 nights), and occupancy thresholds per room tier (Standard: max 2, Deluxe: max 4, Suite: max 6).

Dynamic Pricing: Calculates base rates via switch control structures ($50–$130/night).

Custom Adjustments: Applies progressive multi-night stay discounts (5%–12%), per-guest breakfast add-ons, large group surcharges (>4 guests), and senior citizen discounts (age 60+).

2. ✈️ Airline Ticket Booking System

Eligibility Validation: Enforces baggage limits (max 50kg) and restricts passengers under 12 from booking First Class seats.

Fare & Discount Structure: Supports Multi-ticket group discounts (5%–10%), child fare reductions (20%), senior discounts (10%), travel insurance add-ons ($25/ticket), and extra baggage weight calculations.

3. 🚗 Vehicle Rental Management System

Driver Eligibility: Verifies age thresholds (21+ for standard vehicles, 25+ for Luxury) and minimum driving experience constraints.

Cost Calculations: Integrates daily rental rates ($35–$100/day), duration discounts (7+ days), optional collision/daily insurance ($15/day), and young-driver surcharges (ages 21–24).

4. 🎓 University Course Registration Fee System

Course & Level Pricing: Computes tuition fees based on academic year levels ($40–$55 per course unit) across 1 to 8 enrolled courses.

Services & Bundle Discounts: Integrates accommodation ($120) and transport ($50) fees with conditional bundle discounts for high-volume course enrollments.

🛠️ Technical Concepts & Architecture

UI/UX Containers: Standardized layout design utilizing GroupBox, ListBox, DateTimePicker, NumericUpDown, RadioButton, and CheckBox controls for organized user data entry.

Safe Parsing & Input Validation: Built-in safe data parsing using int.TryParse() and double.TryParse() to prevent runtime exceptions from malformed inputs.

Control Flow: Nested if-else conditional branches, switch blocks, and boolean flags to govern application approval workflows.

Output Formatting: Clean representation of computed summaries and financial figures using currency string formats (:C / ToString()).

🚀 Getting Started

Prerequisites

Visual Studio 2022 (or Visual Studio 2019) with the .NET Desktop Development workload installed.

.NET Framework / .NET Core Runtime.

Running the Application

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/Eng-Rahma-Nor/CSharp-Course.git


Open AssignmentOne.sln or firstassign.csproj in Visual Studio.

Build the solution (Ctrl + Shift + B).

Press F5 or click Start to run the application.

📋 Control Conventions

txt... : TextBox inputs (e.g., txtGuestName, txtAge)

rdo... : RadioButtons for mutually exclusive options (e.g., rdoEconomy, rdoSUV)

chk... : CheckBoxes for optional features (e.g., chkInsurance)

lst... / lbl... : Output targets for summary views (e.g., lstResults)